Hmm, actually `.map((entry) => ({ ...entry, ordinal: ... }))` copies `tip` into the entry, then final map picks three fields. Slight waste but clear. I'll simplify by computing ordinal in the final map instead:

```ts
const owned = listed
  .map((entry) => ({ ...entry, ordinal: ordinalOfBranch(entry.name, issueNumber) }))
  .filter((entry) => entry.ordinal > 0);
const branches = owned.map((entry) => ({
  name: entry.name,
